// ═══════════════════════════════  PORTFOLIO  ════════════════════════════
// The last word: how much, and whether at all. It reads the intention the
// strategy published and turns it into an order, or refuses it.
//
// Two concerns, kept apart because they answer different questions:
//
//   Risk management — how much this position may lose. The strategy says
//   where the stop is; the distance to it and the risk allowed decide the
//   size. Changing how risk is taken happens here, once, for every
//   strategy there will ever be.
//
//   Position manager — whether this one may be opened. What is already
//   running is not something a strategy can see, so rules that depend on
//   the book live here: no pyramiding, a ceiling on open positions, a stop
//   for the day. A strategy that carried its own copy of those would
//   eventually be the one missing a rule.
//
// This is the only layer besides the strategy that the indicator does not
// share. There are no positions to manage in an indicator.
//
// Empty until the rules are specified.
